To assemble, link and load example.asm:
  chmod +x asm64 (this will only need to be done once)
  ./asm64 example (the .asm extension is added by the asm64 bash script file)

To run the debugger input file, which will also start the program,
add breakpoints, and display the outputs you specify:
  gdb example (this will start the debugger - you could also do 'ddd example')
  then at the (gdb prompt)
  source gdbIn.txt

To assemble, link, and load scratch.asm
  ./asm64 scratch
Then to debug
  gdb scratch
Set a breakpoint
  break last
Run the program
  run
